Swap key and value by writing {v: k for k, v in d.items()}.

code:
d = {"a": 1, "b": 2}
inv = {v: k for k, v in d.items()}
print(inv)  # {1: 'a', 2: 'b'}

real example:
Turning a name-to-ID map into an ID-to-name map for reverse lookups.

Each value is doubled while keys stay the same.

code:
d = {"a": 1, "b": 2}
print({k: v * 2 for k, v in d.items()})  # {'a': 2, 'b': 4}

real example:
Applying a double points bonus to every member's current points.
